  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Novel products that improve broiler health and reduce antibiotics usage</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kanters Special Products B.V. (Kanters) focuses on improving animal health through drinking water and reducing the use of antibiotics. Kanters does this, by accurately adding liquid nutritional supplements developed by them to the drinking water. Kanters products are most effective when poultry farms receive healthy &apos;high-quality day-old-chicks&apos; (DOC) from the hatcheries.In the Philippines, most day-old-chicks suffer from dehydration, stress and high temperatures, 24 to 72 hours after hatching in the hatchery. This has a major negative impact on the growth performance of the birds during the remaining life cycle on the broiler farms.Kanters wants to collaborate with Royal Pas Reform B.V..Pas Reform provides total solutions for hatcheries and has developed the SmartStart system: an early feeding system for hatcheries that greatly improves the quality of newly hatched chicks through quick access to feed, water and light which results in a significantly lower mortality in the first week and which helps to limit the use of antibiotics.In the Philippines, the use of antibiotics in livestock farming is excessive and is used preventively by almost all livestock farmers. This entails many risks, of which resistance is the most important.The aim of the demonstration project is to convince local poultry farmers, active in breeding, hatching and keeping broilers, to invest in Kanters and Pas Reform products by demonstrating the benefits of the combined technologies. The aim is to demonstrate that the technologies not only lead to better animal health and a reduction in medication and antibiotic use, but also to better business results for poultry farmers.</narrative>
  </description>
